    "text": "BE \u00d0AM GEBRO\u00d0RUM \u00d0E FEOR FRAM CYRICEAN WYRCA\u00d0.\n\u00dea gebro\u00f0ra, \u00fee feorr beo\u00f0 on geswince and hig ne magon for \u00f0am fyrlene on gedafenlicum tidum\nDon handswagelice \u00fea, \u00f0e on fare synd, and hig na forgiman \u00fea gesettan tida, ac \u00e6lcne tidsang\nBE \u00deAM GEBRO\u00d0RUM \u00deE ON FARE SYND.\n\u00dea gebro\u00f0ra, \u00fee for hwylcere neode utfara\u00f0 and hig \u00feam ylcan d\u00e6ge to mynstre cuman magon, ne\nGif hit hwa \u00f0onne de\u00f0 butan his leafe, beo on amansumunge.\nBE MYNSTRES GEBEDHUSE.\nGebedhus sig to \u00f0am anum, \u00fee hit gecweden is, \u00fe\u00e6t is, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r nan \u00f0ing elles geworht sig o\u00f0\u00f0e\n\u00c6t \u00e6lces tidsanges ende gan hig ut ealle mid \u00fe\u00e6re m\u00e6stan swigan and sig God a gewur\u00f0od \u00fe\u00e6t se\nGif hwylc heora eft onsundron hine diglice gebiddan wyle, he inga mid stilnysse and hine gebidde,\nEornostlice se, \u00f0e \u00feyllice weorc \u00fe\u00e6rinne wyrcan nelle, ne ge\u00feafige man him, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00f0\u00e6rinne\nBE CUMENA ANDFENGE.\nEalle cuman, \u00fee to mynstre cuma\u00f0, underfo man hig, swylce hit Crist sylf sig, for\u00f0am \u00fee he sylf\nFor\u00f0ig eornostlice, sona swa se cuma gecydd sig, gange se ealdor him togeanes, o\u00f0\u00fee \u00fea gebro\u00f0ra,\nNe beode him mann sibbecoss, \u00e6r\u00f0am \u00fee hig to Gode gebiddan and bletsunge underfon, for\nOn \u00fe\u00e6re gem\u00e6nnan gretinge beo \u00fe\u00e6r eall eadmodnyss \u00e6teowed eallum cuman, \u00fee to mynstre\nBeon hig to cyrcan gel\u00e6dde to gebede, and underfon hig sy\u00f0\u00f0an, swa swa him to gebyra\u00f0; sitte\nBeo ger\u00e6dd \u00e6tforan \u00feam cuman seo godcunde \u00e6 and lar, \u00fe\u00e6t he sig getrymmed to Godes willan,\nAbrece se abbod his f\u00e6sten for cumena \u00feingon, butan hit hwylc healic f\u00e6sten sig, \u00fee man abrecan\nGeote se abbod w\u00e6ter \u00feam cuman to handum; \u00fewean eallra cumena fet, \u00e6g\u00f0er ge se abbod ge\n\u00c6fter \u00feam \u00f0weale singe man \u00feis fers \u00f0us cwe\u00f0ende: Suscipiamus domine misericordiam tuam\nBeo \u00f0am abbode seo m\u00e6ste hogu \u00fe\u00e6s andfencges \u00feearfena and el\u00f0eodigra, for\u00f0am Cristus on hig\nBeo \u00fe\u00e6s abbodes kicene and \u00f0\u00e6ra cumena onsundron, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0a gebro\u00f0ra ne beon geunstilde, \u00feonne\nTo geares f\u00e6ce twegen gebro\u00f0ra into cumena kicenan gan, and \u00fea beon swylce, \u00fee wel cunnon\nBeo him geseald fultum, gif hig \u00fe\u00e6s behofia\u00f0, \u00f0\u00e6t hig \u00f0urh \u00fe\u00e6s fultumes frofor butan ceorunge\n\u00d0eos foresceawung sig gehealden na on \u00feisum anum, ac on eallum mynster\u00feenungum, \u00fe\u00e6t is,\nSig cumena hus swylcum bre\u00f0er bet\u00e6ht to bewitenne, \u00fee fullne Geodes ege h\u00e6bbe and his sawle\nNateshwon heora nan wi\u00f0 cumena hine geferl\u00e6ce o\u00f0\u00f0e \u00e6ninge spr\u00e6ce wi\u00f0 hine h\u00e6bbe, butan \u00feam\nBE \u00deAM \u00de\u00c6T NAN MUNUC \u00c6RENDGEWRITU NE O\u00deRE LAC NE UNDERFO.\nNe sig nateshwon munece alyfed, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00e6nig gewrit o\u00f0\u00f0e sende, o\u00f0\u00f0e lac underfon fram heora\nGif hw\u00e6t heora \u00e6nigum fram heora magum asend by\u00f0, ne gedyrstl\u00e6ce he hit na to underfonne,\nGif hit \u00feonne se abbod underfon hate, stande on his dome, hwam hit man sylle; and se bro\u00f0or, \u00fee\nSe \u00f0e o\u00f0erlicor gedyrstl\u00e6ce, underhnige \u00fe\u00e6re regollican steore.\nBE MYNSTERMANNA HR\u00c6GELHUSE AND HYRA HR\u00c6GELTALE.\nSig gebro\u00f0rum reaf geseald be swylcnysse and sta\u00f0ele \u00fe\u00e6re stowe, \u00fee hig onwunia\u00f0, and be \u00fe\u00e6s\n\u00de\u00e6s abbodes foresceawung sceal beon be \u00feisum, hu \u00fe\u00e6s neodige.\nWe \u00feeah gelyfa\u00f0, on medemum stowum \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6nlipigeum munecum genihtsumige, \u00fe\u00e6t he h\u00e6bbe\nNe cidon \u00fea munecas ymbe \u00fea deage o\u00f0\u00f0e greatnysse heora reafa; habbon swylce reaf, swylce\nBesceawige se abbod and hate besidian \u00fe\u00e6re reafa gemet, \u00fe\u00e6t hig ne beon to sceorte, ac gem\u00e6te\nAgife a \u00fea ealdan, \u00feonne him man niwe reaf sylle, and to hr\u00e6gelhuse bet\u00e6con, \u00feearfum to d\u00e6lene.\nGenoh by\u00f0 \u00feam munuce and fullgenihstum, \u00fe\u00e6t he h\u00e6bbe twa culan and twegen syricas for \u00f0\u00e6re\nSwa oft, swa hig a\u00f0or o\u00f0\u00f0e meon, o\u00f0\u00f0e \u00e6nig \u00feing niwes underfon, bet\u00e6can a \u00fe\u00e6t ealde.\n\u00d0a \u00fee on ytinge fara\u00f0 ahwyder, niman him brec of hr\u00e6gelhuse, eft swa hig cumon ham of \u00f0am\nBeon eac on hr\u00e6glhuse gehealden \u00e6g\u00f0er ge culan ge syricas \u00e6thwega beteran \u00feonne \u00f0a, \u00fee hig\nTo beddreafe genihtsumige to h\u00e6bbenne meatte and hwitel and beddfelt and heafodbolstor.\n\u00d0eahhw\u00e6\u00f0ere se abbod sceal gelomlice sceawian \u00fea bedd and asmeagan for syndrigum \u00e6htum.\nGif hig hwa h\u00e6bbe, o\u00f0\u00f0e.\nBE MYNSTRES CR\u00c6FTIGAN.\nGif cr\u00e6ftige menn on mynstre beon, began \u00feone cr\u00e6ft and georne wyrcan, gif hit se abbod\nGif hwylc heora for \u00f0\u00e6s cr\u00e6ftes \u00feingon hine onhef\u00f0, for \u00fe\u00e6s cr\u00e6ftes truwan and for\u00f0ig, \u00f0e he\nGif man hw\u00e6t becypan sceole, \u00fe\u00e6s \u00f0e cr\u00e6ftige menn on mynstre wyrca\u00f0, warnian \u00fea, \u00f0e \u00feone\nBeon hig gemyndig symble Annaniam and Saphiram, \u00feel\u00e6s \u00f0e hig \u00feone dea\u00f0 on heora sawle\nGif hwylc neod sig to becypenne \u00e6nig \u00feincg heore handcr\u00e6ftes, \u00fe\u00e6t sig butan gitsunge undeoror\nBE NICUMENRA GEBRO\u00d0RA ANDFENCGE.\nGif hwa niwan to mynstres drohtnunge gecyrran wyle, ne sig him na ea\u00f0elic \u00fe\u00e6s inf\u00e6res geti\u00f0od;\nGif he ge\u00f0yldelice forbyr\u00f0 \u00e6g\u00f0er ge hosp ge edwit, and on \u00f0\u00e6re wirne \u00feeah \u00feurhwuna\u00f0 and\nT\u00e6ce him man sy\u00f0\u00f0an to nigcumenra manna huse, and he \u00f0\u00e6r ete and reste and embe his\nAnd gastlic ealdor and wis his h\u00e6bbe gymene, \u00fee wel cunne sawla Gode gestrynan, se geornlice\nBeo him ges\u00e6d eall seo sti\u00f0nys and earfo\u00f0nys, \u00fee to Gode l\u00e6t and to heofenan rices gefean.\nGif he \u00feonn beh\u00e6t sta\u00f0olf\u00e6stnysse, \u00fe\u00e6t he on \u00f0am \u00feurhwunian wylle, embe twegen mon\u00f0as\nGif he \u00feonne gyt \u00feurhwuna\u00f0, l\u00e6de hine man eft to nicumenra manna huse, and his man georne\nEft embe syx mon\u00feas sig him ger\u00e6dd eall \u00fees regol fram foreweardan, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00f0e geornlicor\nGif he \u00feonne gyt \u00feurhwuna\u00f0, embe feower mon\u00f0as sig him eft \u00fees ylca regol ger\u00e6dd and \u00fe\u00e6t\nGif he \u00feonne be his agenum dome beh\u00e6t, \u00fe\u00e6t he ealle \u00f0incg gehealdan wylle and ealle \u00fe\u00e6s regoles\nWite he eac, \u00fe\u00e6t he mid \u00f0\u00e6s regoles bendum swa by\u00f0 getiged and gesta\u00f0elod, \u00fe\u00e6t he of \u00f0am\nSy\u00f0\u00f0an he underfangen sig and innan cyrcan gebroht, behate he beforan eallre geferr\u00e6dene Gode\nGif he \u00feonne ahw\u00e6nne \u00feis behat abryc\u00f0, wite he, \u00fe\u00e6t he by\u00f0 geny\u00f0erod and gehynod fram\nBe \u00feam his behate sette he f\u00e6stnunga mid gewrite to \u00f0\u00e6s abbodes naman and \u00f0\u00e6ra halgena, \u00fee\nWrite he \u00f0a f\u00e6stnunga mid his agenre handa, gif he \u00feonne writan ne cunne, bidde o\u00f0erne, \u00fee\nSona swa he \u00fe\u00e6t gewrit uppan \u00f0am altare lecge, beginne \u00feis fers and \u00f0us cwe\u00fee: Suscipe me,\n\u00d0\u00e6t ylce fers he sceal \u00feriwa cwe\u00f0an and eall geferr\u00e6den \u00feriwa mid \u00f0am ilcan ferse andswarian\nSe sylfa nicumena bro\u00f0or, sy\u00f0\u00f0an he gehalgod by\u00f0, gefealle \u00e6lces \u00e6nlypiges fet and \u00fe\u00e6s\nGif he hwylce \u00e6hta h\u00e6bbe, o\u00f0\u00f0e hig on \u00e6r \u00feearfum d\u00e6le, o\u00f0\u00f0e arwyr\u00f0lice mid him sylfum \u00f0am\nUnscyrde hine man sona and \u00fea reaf nime, \u00fee he \u00e6r notode, and hine mid mynstres reafum\nHealde man on hr\u00e6gelhuse \u00f0a reaf, \u00fee he him of adyde, to\u00feig, gif he ahw\u00e6nne \u00feurh deofles\nHealde man \u00feeah \u00e6fre \u00fe\u00e6t gewrit his f\u00e6stnunge on \u00feam mynstre.\nBE RICRA MANNA AND \u00deEARFENA BEARNA ANDFENCGE.\nGif hwylc rice mann and \u00e6\u00f0elboren his bearn Gode on mynstre geoffrian wyle, gif \u00fe\u00e6t cild \u00fe\u00e6s\nBehaton \u00fea magas and mid a\u00fee gef\u00e6stnian, \u00fe\u00e6t hig n\u00e6fre syndrige \u00e6hta heora m\u00e6ge ne\nGif hig \u00feonne hw\u00e6t wyllon syllon, syllon hig \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6re halgon stowe to rihtum gem\u00e6nscipe,\nBeon ealle \u00fea \u00e6hta, \u00fee \u00f0am cilde gebyrige, swa fordilegode and tod\u00e6lede, \u00fe\u00e6t him nan hiht beon\nDo handswagelice be heora bearnum, \u00fea \u00f0e unrice synd and hafenlease \u00feearfan.\nGif hig nane \u00e6hta to syllenne nabban, offrian heora bearn andfealdlice on gewittnysse\nBE ABBODUM AND O\u00deRUM GE\u00deUNGENUM \u00deE MENSTRES GEWILNIA\u00d0.\nGif hwylc m\u00e6ssepreost gewilna\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t hine man to munuchade to mynstre underfo, ne sig him\nGif he \u00feonne \u00f0urhwuna\u00f0 on \u00feissere gewilnunge, ne sig nan \u00f0ing forl\u00e6ten, \u00f0\u00e6s \u00f0e se regol t\u00e6ce\n\u00de\u00e6t is on andgite: com \u00feu mid sibbe and mid so\u00f0re abryrdnesse, \u00fee mid unge\u00few\u00e6rnysse and\nSig him ge\u00f0afod, \u00fe\u00e6t he stede \u00e6fter \u00f0am abbode healde and \u00fe\u00e6t he m\u00e6ssan sincge, gif se abbod\nBeo he symble gearu to \u00e6lcere steore be regoles t\u00e6cinge, and swa he eadmodra beo, swa\nGif he for his hades arwur\u00f0nysse fur\u00f0or forl\u00e6ten sig, ne gedyrstl\u00e6ce he on nanre fandunge \u00feurh\n\u00d0a \u00f0e clerichades synd and munuchades wilnia\u00f0, beon hig underfangene on medemum stedum,\nBE \u00c6L\u00deEODIGUM MUNUCUM HU HI MAN UNDERFON SCEAL.\nSe utacymena munuc, \u00fee of uncu\u00f0um eardum cym\u00f0, gif he on cumena hiwe wunian wylle and\nGif he sceadelice mid eadmodnysse and mid so\u00f0re lufe hwylc \u00feincg on mynstre astelle o\u00f0\u00f0e\nGif he eft on \u00e6nigne timan hine sylfne to mynstres wununge gef\u00e6stnian wyle, ne onscunige\nGif man \u00e6nigne un\u00f0eaw on him agitt o\u00f0\u00f0e onfint on his cumli\u00f0nysse, ne sceal he habban nane\nGif he \u00f0anne swa anr\u00e6de by\u00f0 on \u00fe\u00e6re cumli\u00f0nysse, \u00fe\u00e6t he wur\u00f0e ne beo, \u00fe\u00e6t he beo \u00feanon\nGif se abbod his geearnunga swa agitt, he hine mot be sumum d\u00e6le fur\u00f0or wyr\u00feian and him innor\nNis na \u00feis be munecum anum to healdene, ac eac be arwur\u00f0um canonicum, \u00fee to munuclife\nWarnige se abbod \u00feeahhw\u00e6\u00f0ere, \u00fe\u00e6t he nateshwon of nanum cu\u00f0um mynstre munuc ne underfo\nBE MYNSTRES SACERDUM.\nGif hwylc abbod m\u00e6ssepreostes behofige o\u00f0\u00f0e diacones, geceose he of his agenum geferum \u00fee\nSy\u00f0\u00f0an he \u00feonne gehadod sig, warnige hine georne wi\u00f0 modinysse and to\u00feundenre\nNe he \u00feurh \u00f0one truwan his sacerdhades ofergapige his gehyrsumnysse and \u00fea steore \u00fe\u00e6s halgan\nHealde he symble \u00feone stede and \u00fea endebyrdnysse his gecyrrednysse, butan \u00f0\u00e6re \u00feenunge anre\nWite he \u00feeah, \u00fe\u00e6t he sig a under\u00feeodd \u00feam halgan regole and his yldrum, and \u00e6lc \u00feing do and\nGif he \u00feurh dyrstignysse \u00feonne hine onhef\u00f0 mid modignysse, ne beo he na sacerd geteald ac\nGif he \u00feonne \u00f0urh mynegunge nele beon gerihtl\u00e6ht, hit stande \u00feonne on \u00f0\u00e6s bisceopes dome.\nGif he \u00feonne gyt gebetan nelle \u00e6t openum gylte and he \u00feurh his modignysse nelle beon\nBE EALLE GEFERES ENDEBYRDNYSSE.\n\u00c6lc endebyrdnys on mynstre sceal beon gehealden and gefadod be heora gecyrrednysse and be\nSe abbod ne geunstille, ne ne gedrefe \u00fea heorde, \u00f0e him under\u00f0eodd is, ne he nan \u00feincg ne\n\u00c6fter \u00fe\u00e6re endebyrdnysse, \u00fee se abbod gesta\u00f0ela\u00f0 and \u00f0a gebro\u00f0ru him betwynan healda\u00f0,\nOn nanum stowum ne beo seo endebyrdnys be nanre ylde gefadod, ne seo yld \u00fea iugo\u00f0e ne\nFor\u00f0ig \u00feonne, butan \u00f0am anum, \u00f0e for heora leahtrum of heora endebyrdnysse uttor ascofene\n\u00dea gingran for\u00f0ig arwur\u00f0ian heora yldran, and \u00fea yldran lufian heora gingran.\nNe gedyrstl\u00e6ce heora nan, \u00fe\u00e6t he o\u00f0erne his agenum naman synderlice genemne, ac \u00f0a yldran\nSe abbod for\u00f0ig, \u00fee he Godes gespelia is, sig hlaford gehaten and f\u00e6der, na for his agenum\n\u00d0ence he symble and on goddere drohtnunge hine swa gearwige, \u00fe\u00e6t he sig wyr\u00f0e swa myccles\nSwa hw\u00e6r swa gebro\u00f0ra hig gemeton, bidde se gingra bletsunge \u00e6t \u00feam yldran.\nEft gif se yldra g\u00e6\u00f0 for\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6r se gingra sitt, arise se gingra mid eadmodnysse and \u00feam yldran to\nNe dyrstl\u00e6ce se gingra, \u00fe\u00e6t he mid \u00feam yldran sitte, butan he hine hate, \u00fe\u00e6t symble beo\n\u00d0a cild and seo geogu\u00f0 mid steore and \u00feeawf\u00e6stnysse heora endebyrdnysse healdon, ge on\nBE \u00de\u00c6S ABBUDES HADUNGE.\nOn abbodes hadunge is swy\u00f0e to besceawigenne mid mycclum gesceade, \u00fe\u00e6t se beo to abbode\nGif eall geferr\u00e6den \u00feone r\u00e6d on gem\u00e6num ge\u00feeahte missr\u00e6da\u00f0 and \u00feeah feawa witena on \u00f0am\nNe \u00f0a o\u00fere ongean \u00fe\u00e6t nan \u00f0incg wi\u00f0cwe\u00f0on.\n\u00c6fter his lifes geearnunga and \u00e6fter his wisdomes lare sig gecoren, se \u00f0e to abbodhade sceal, eac\nGif hit \u00f0onne swa getima\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t eall geferr\u00e6den anmodum ge\u00feeahte \u00f0one to abbode gecyst, \u00fee\nWite \u00e6g\u00f0er ge bisceop, ge \u00fea rihtgelyfedan, \u00fe\u00e6t hig mycele mede \u00e6t Gode habba\u00f0, gif hig mid\n\u00d0ence se abbod, sy\u00f0\u00f0an he gehadod by\u00f0, hu mycele byr\u00f0ene and hu hefigtyme he underfencg\nEornostlice him gedafena\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t he wel gel\u00e6red sig mid godcundre \u00e6 and to \u00feam snoter, \u00fe\u00e6t he\nSig he cl\u00e6ne and syfre and mildheort, and beo a seo mildheortnys wyldre \u00f0onne se rihta dom,\nHatige \u00f0a leahtras and lufige \u00f0a gebro\u00f0ra.\nBeo he snotor and wel besceawod on \u00feeawum and na oferswi\u00f0e ne ge\u00fereage, \u00feel\u00e6s \u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6t omige\nNe t\u00e6ce we na mid swa geradum bysnungum and gebeorhlicum larum, \u00fe\u00e6t he leahtras fyr\u00f0rige\nHicge he and gecneordl\u00e6ce, \u00fe\u00e6t hine man lufian m\u00e6ge, swi\u00f0or \u00feonne ondr\u00e6dan.\nNe beo he drefende ne angmod, ne he ne beo to swi\u00f0 ne annwille, ne he ne beo andig and f\u00e6cne,\nBeo he a foregleaw and wel besceawod on his bebodum; \u00e6g\u00f0er ge \u00e6fter godcundum \u00feincgum\nBeo he gemyndig \u00fea gesceadwisnysse Sancte Jacobes, \u00fe\u00e6s heahf\u00e6deres, \u00f0e \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0: Gif ic\nNime him \u00f0a bysene and o\u00f0re swylce \u00f0\u00e6s so\u00fean gesceades, \u00fee is eallra m\u00e6gna modor, and swa\n\u00d0onne he wel \u00f0ena\u00fe and ures drihtnes heorde cwiferlice gealga\u00f0 and to rihte mana\u00f0, he",
